✅ Protecting Azure Infrastructure Using CSPM, SIEM, and XDR
Implemented multiple security solutions to continuously monitor, detect, and respond to cyber threats.
1. CSPM (Cloud Security Posture Management)
	• Continuously monitors cloud resources for:
		○ Misconfigurations
		○ Security vulnerabilities
		○ Policy violations
		○ Potential threats
	• Performs automated remediation such as:
		○ Fixing insecure configurations
		○ Deploying vulnerability scanners
		○ Installing log collection agents and AV/AM sensors
	• Ensures compliance with industry standards and internal security policies.

2. XDR (Extended Detection and Response)
	• Collects and correlates security data from multiple sources:
		○ Endpoints (servers and user devices)
		○ Network logs
		○ Azure Monitor
		○ CSPM tools
		○ Identity systems (Microsoft Entra ID)
		○ Azure Activity Logs
	• Provides a centralized and holistic security view.
	• Uses machine learning and analytics to detect suspicious behavior and hidden threats.
	• Supports automated incident investigation and response workflows.

3. SIEM (Security Information and Event Management)
	• Provides:
		○ Centralized logging and monitoring
		○ Data correlation
		○ Reporting and compliance tracking
	• Collects logs from multiple tools including CSPM, XDR, CASB, EDR, and other systems.
	• Maintains a complete audit trail of security events.
	• Identifies patterns and trends to improve threat detection.
	• Generates compliance and regulatory reports.

Differences Between CSPM, XDR, and SIEM
	• CSPM: Prevents risks by enforcing best practices and fixing misconfigurations.
	• XDR: Detects and investigates threats using real-time analytics.
	• SIEM: Centralizes visibility, investigation, and compliance reporting.

Benefits of Implementing These Solutions
	• ✅ Reduced risk of successful cyber-attacks through proactive detection and response.
	• ✅ Improved operational efficiency via automated investigations.
	• ✅ Enhanced compliance through continuous monitoring and reporting.

